    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 4 and takes about 45 minutes. The thing to watch is the palm oil temperature at the start: heat it gently until just melted but do not let it reach its smoke point or the stew will taste bitter and the colour will darken too much."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spinach is used here as the most widely available substitute for kontomire. Fresh spinach makes a lighter stew; frozen spinach works equally well and gives a more concentrated leafy flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "spinach",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
